  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>
    The morning is when your cortisol is highest, your motivation circuits are most
    responsive, and your environment is most controllable. The men who consistently build
    health across the 4M program share one behavioral trait more than any other:
    a structured morning that doesn't depend on motivation to execute.
  </p>
  <p>
    The 4M morning protocol is designed to be completed in 45–60 minutes and serves as
    the daily on-ramp for all four pillars — not just Muscle. Light exposure, movement,
    hydration, protein intake, and a brief Mind practice compound powerfully over months.
  </p>

  <h2>Our approach</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Light + Movement Block</h3>
      <p>Outdoor light within 30 minutes of waking + 10 minutes of mobility work. Sets circadian tone for the day.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Hydration & Minerals</h3>
      <p>32oz water + electrolytes before coffee. Simple, almost universally neglected, measurably impactful.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Protein-Forward Breakfast</h3>
      <p>40g+ protein at the first meal. Anchors muscle protein synthesis and reduces afternoon appetite drift.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>2-Minute Mind Practice</h3>
      <p>Intention-setting or box breathing. Keeps the Mind pillar present even on compressed mornings.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

